        {
          "widget": {
            "name": "3ab86a30",
            "multilineTextboxSpec": {
              "lines": [
                "# Seller Acquisition Channel Performance\n",
                "\n",
                "Olist sellers who signed by June 2, 2018 (667), measured over their first 90 days. **Paid search sellers are about 17 points more likely to start selling than organic search sellers; once active, sellers perform the same regardless of channel.**"
              ]
            }
          },
          "position": {
            "x": 0,
            "y": 0,
            "width": 12,
            "height": 2
          }
        },
        {
          "widget": {
            "name": "d66a1fbd",
            "multilineTextboxSpec": {
              "lines": [
                "### Key findings\n",
                "\n",
                "- **Channel affects activation, not performance.** Paid search sellers activate at 54.8% vs. 38.9% for organic search (odds ratio 2.15 after controls, p = 0.001). Revenue, reviews, and delivery do not differ by channel.\n",
                "- **Seller type matters more than channel.** Large online sellers activate at 62% vs. 25% for offline businesses; resellers at 49% vs. 32% for manufacturers.\n",
                "- **Break-even:** paid search can cost up to about 41% more per acquired seller than organic and still match its cost per active seller (95% CI: 12% to 78%).\n",
                "\n",
                "### Caveats\n",
                "\n",
                "Observational data (sellers were not randomly assigned to channels). Small channels have wide confidence intervals. Revenue is highly skewed, so medians are shown. About a quarter of sellers have no recorded channel."
              ]
            }
          },
          "position": {
            "x": 0,
            "y": 21,
            "width": 12,
            "height": 4
          }
        }
